# Building KACTL

Use the Makefile from the repo root (`make help`). Agent-oriented notes: `agents/verify.md`.

## Requirements

- Python 3
- GNU Make
- `pdflatex` (TeX Live: `texlive-latex-base`, `texlive-latex-recommended`, `texlive-latex-extra`, `texlive-plain-generic`, `texlive-fonts-recommended`)
- `g++` and `bc` for compile/stress tests

## Commands

- `make preprocess` — generate `build/listings/**`, `web/public/snippets.json`, and `build/header.tmp.seed` from `content/`.
- `make kactl` — preprocess, build `test-session.pdf`, two-pass PDF → `kactl.pdf`.
- `make fast` — preprocess + one LaTeX pass.
- `make web-pdf` — preprocess + two-pass PDF without test-session (GitHub Pages).
- `make test-preprocess` — unit tests for snippet stripping / chapter parsing.
- `make test-compiles` / `make test` — header compile check and stress tests.

`pdflatex` still needs `-shell-escape` for the running page header (`content/tex/preprocessor.py --print-header`). Snippet listings are not generated inside LaTeX.

## Adding chapters and snippets

1. Add `content/<chapter>/chapter.tex` and source files.
2. Include snippets with `\kactlimport{File.h}` in that `chapter.tex`.
3. Register the chapter with `\kactlchapter{<chapter>}` in `content/kactl.tex`.
4. Annotate C++/Java/Python files with a `/** Author / Description */` header (see `agents/content.md`).

Team name, university, and contest line are in `content/kactl.tex`.
